<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Americas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Americas are the continents of North and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. They were home to indigenous states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> before European conquest and colonisation from 1492, led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> and followed by Portugal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. American <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and plantation economies, worked by enslaved Africans from regions such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a>, transformed global trade, reaching as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/americas.jpg" alt="Americas" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin23230 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Americas_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
